  "details": "While holding a QvPen in hand and holding the Tab key to draw in place in desktop mode, the mouse cursor highlights prints which means the Quick Menu prints UI disruptively in Build `1918` and later where in Build `1902` and earlier it did not. See the attached videos for comparison.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\n1. Launch VRChat in desktop mode.\n\n2. Print something (a \"bingo card\") in a world with a QvPen with VRC+.\n\n3. Grab a QvPen from the world.\n\n4. Go near the print and while standing in place, start drawing on the print with a QvPen while holding the Tab key.\n\nExpected result: When holding an object like a QvPen in hand (which stays in hand without holding the left mouse button), holding the Tab key should not highlight prints. This is the behavior in Build `1902`.\n\nActual result: In build `1918` and later, the print details UI keeps popping up while drawing on a print disruptively while a QvPen is held in hand.\n\nTested with Build `1902` and Build `1921`. (Please note, the drawings on video are for show/testing. Don't read into them too much.)",
